<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to October 16 as released by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.34 (0.34)	 one year     0.40 (0.41)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.34 (0.35)	 two years    0.51 (0.56)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.35 (0.36)	 three years  1.05 (1.10)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.35 (0.36)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.46 (0.51)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.30 (0.31)	 three years  1.00 (1.06)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.31 (0.32)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.41 (0.49)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.26 (0.26)	 three years  0.95 (1.01)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Oct 14 - Oct 18:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.48 (0.48)   120-150 days  0.54 (0.54)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.49 (0.51)   150-180 days  0.53 (0.55)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.51 (0.51)   180-360 days  0.50 (0.57)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.52 (0.52)   over 360 days 0.48 (0.53)</p>
